answers.reconciled:
All three reviewers say the non-legislative elements are not strong enough as written. Their proposals for strengthening them overlap only in part.

claude-opus-5-5 and gpt-6.1-sol both call for:
- a demanding first round at the top, which #7 and #26 do not supply;
- training for all managers, not just SCS;
- funding;
- consolidating the overlapping records and codes.

claude-opus-5-5 also wants:
- a consequence for refusing ownership;
- register data feeding promotion and exit mechanically, for all grades;
- named owners and success tests for each action;
- the pilot's escalation-willingness measure (#35) turned into a culture indicator.

gpt-6.1-sol also wants goals checked for nesting, delegations validated, and a system-first way of handling failures.

gemini-3.1-pro-preview proposes tying budgets directly to the completion of named owners' tasks.
